last month the tampa bay buccaneers  tight end known as grunk retired from  the nfl for the second time the first  time was after nine years with the new  england patriots this sunday gronk will  co-host the usa today high school sports  awards which celebrate the country's  best student athletes earlier he  surprised swimmer claire kerzan from  north carolina with the girls athlete of  the year award take a look  hey claire  hi  what's up it's rob gronkowski here how  you doing  i'm much better now how are you  oh that's good i'm really good i'm just  hanging out  i just want  you know  let you know that you are nominated for  the usa today high school sports awards  girls athlete of the year and you know  i'm hosting the show right  of course i do  so i thought it would be fun to come on  and surprise you here today and i've  been impressed by your high school  career so far you have broken so many  records  at such a young age and on top of all  that  i have some good news for you you aren't  just nominated for the award you are the  winner for girls  here congratulations claire thank you so  much yes pretty incredible how do you  feel about it honestly it's it's an  honor um i know there was a huge list of  incredibly you know acclaimed uh kids so  to think that you know i'm  pretty good too i it's an honor yeah  really congratulations to you claire for  being named girls athlete of the year it  is an honor i know how much work uh goes  into it how much dedication and uh it's  just starting now you got your whole  life out of you and uh you're going to  make dreams come true  oh i really hope so thank you so much  rob gronkowski joins us right now grunk  what's up baby how you doing nate man  what's good man i'm doing well how are  you  i'm good good to have you now listen you  remember being a high school athlete  with your whole life in front of you  what is it like to give out these awards  to these high school student athletes  uh it's really special i mean 